course: dictionary
lesson: 5560
title: Lengthways and across
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lengthways tells you the direction of a cut, fold or line. It means along the longest side of something, from one end to the other. The opposite is across, from one side to the other.
explain: «Cut the carrot lengthways into long strips.» The cuts run along the long side of the carrot, so each strip is long and thin. If the cuts went across, you would get short round pieces instead.
explain: In maths, direction changes the shape of the pieces. «A rectangle cut in half lengthways makes two long thin rectangles.» Ask yourself: which side is the longest? The cut runs along that side.
explain: To check a word like this, swap in your meaning: «Cut the carrot from end to end, along the long side.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Lengthways means along the longest side of something, from end to end.
fact: The opposite of lengthways is across, from one side to the other.
fact: Lengthwise is another word with the same meaning as lengthways.
fact: «Fold lengthways» means fold the paper along its long side, so it makes a long thin shape.
fact: «Grapes are cut lengthways for small children, because small round food can block a small child's airway.» Cutting grapes this way is a safety step.
exercise: «Cut the carrot lengthways into long strips.» What does lengthways mean here? | *Along the longest side, from end to end | Into small round pieces | Very quickly | Across, from one side to the other
exercise: «A rectangle cut in half lengthways makes two long thin rectangles.» Which way is the cut? | *Along the long side | Around the edge | Into four equal squares | Across the short side
exercise: «Cut grapes lengthways for small children.» Why are grapes cut this way? | Because lengthways is the fastest way to cut | Because it makes the grapes look nicer | Because grapes are sweeter that way | *Because small round food can block a small child's airway
test: Lengthways means which direction? | Across the shortest side | Straight up | Round in a circle | *Along the longest side
test: Which word means the same as lengthways? | Across | *Lengthwise | Upside down | Sideways, to the left
exam: Ella cuts a long banana lengthways into strips. Which way does each cut run? | *Along the long side, end to end | Around the banana in a circle | Into two small balls | Across the banana
